@title Staff Password and MFA FAQ
@subtitle Cinder Valley School District IT, policy effective 2026-11-03
@author IT team, Cinder Valley School District

This FAQ explains the new staff password and multi-factor authentication policy, which takes effect on 2026-11-03. Read it before the change, and bring your questions to the help desk.

!! IT will never ask for your password or your code by email or phone.

## Why are we changing the policy?

Two phishing incidents in 2026 compromised staff mailboxes. The new policy makes those accounts much harder to break into.

## What changes on November 3?

Passwords must be at least 14 characters long. Every staff account also needs multi-factor authentication.

## Do I have to change my password every 90 days?

No. We are removing forced rotation. We will only ask you to change your password after a suspected compromise.

## What if I do not have a smartphone?

The help desk will issue a hardware key at no cost.

## What if I lose my phone or key?

Call the help desk at extension 4400. They will give you a temporary bypass code, valid for 24 hours.

## Who do I contact for help?

Contact the help desk. It is open from 07:00 to 17:00 on school days.
